# ─── Databases ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SQLite databases are ignored by default...
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# ...except the seeded analytical database, which is COMMITTED ON PURPOSE.
# It is the project's only copy of the ~17,200 cleaned CIHI rows: schema.sql
# creates the tables but leaves them empty, and load_csv.py cannot refill them
# (it reads data/optimized/, which does not exist). Deleting this file leaves
# every dashboard, hypothesis test, and chart with no data.
# See README.md → "Database & Data Provenance".
!backend/database/healthcare.db

# Local working notes on data/statistics defects — not for distribution.
MEMORY.md

# ─── Claude Code ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CLAUDE.md, .claude/CLAUDE.md, .claude/settings.json and .claude/skills/ are
# COMMITTED ON PURPOSE so the graphify setup and project instructions reach the
# whole team. Keep settings.json portable: invoke tools by name (`graphify ...`)
# and resolve them via PATH. An absolute path such as C:/Users/<you>/.local/bin
# makes every PreToolUse hook fail on a teammate's machine.
#
# These two stay local:
#   worktrees/          throwaway agent workspaces, and each is itself a git repo.
#                       Committing one stores a gitlink, so a clone gets an empty
#                       directory pointing at a workspace that no longer exists.
#   settings.local.json machine-specific permissions, per-developer by convention.
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/settings.local.json

# graphify's generated knowledge graph. Regenerated from source by `/graphify .`
# and refreshed with `graphify update .`, so it is derived data: large, and it would
# conflict on nearly every merge. Each developer builds their own.
graphify-out/
